spans.s:
प्रत्यग्रह प्रत्यग्रह, अस्, m., N. of a son
of Vasu and king of the Cedis (= प्रत्य्-अग्र;
probably a contracted form for प्रत्यग्-ग्रह).

प्रत्यर्धि प्रत्य्-अर्धि, इस्, इस्, इ (connected
with अर्ध), Ved. possessing half of (with gen.)?;
having equal claims, equal.

); annoyance, disagreeableness; dis-
appointment, disarrangement; offence, sin, sinfulness;
disappearance of anything that exists; non-production
of what does not exist.

प्रत्यालीढ प्रत्य्-आलीढ, अस्, आ, अम्, eaten;
extended towards the left; (अम्), n. an attitude in shoot-
ing, the left foot advanced and right drawn back.

प्रत्युदि प्रत्य्-उद्-इ (प्रति-), cl. 2. P. -एति,
-एतुम्, to rise and go towards, to go out towards;
to ascend.

प्रत्य्-उद्यमिन् or प्रत्य्-उद्यामिन्, ई, इनी, इ,
Ved. maintaining an equipoise, counterbalancing;
resisting, refractory.

प्रत्युद्या प्रत्य्-उद्-या, cl. 2. P. -याति, -यातुम्,
to rise up and go towards or against, rise to meet;
to go out to meet, go to meet.

प्रत्युपहार प्रत्य्-उपहार, अस्, m. placing
again in any one's hands, giving back, restitution;
(अस्, आ, अम्), handing back, restoring.
